 david@doe.utoronto.ca (David Megginson) writes:

> Here are some suggestions for limiting the power of the ring of
> conflict:

> 1) Have it affect only monsters who respect Elbereth (ie., not @).

> 2) Have it use up much more food than even the ring of regeneration,
> so that anyone wearing it has to eat every 3 or 4 rounds.

> 3) Give every monster a % chance of escaping its effects.

> 4) Make it extremely rare (like named artifacts), so that one usually
> needs a wish to get it.

> There is no need to adapt all of these, any one will probably do.

All good, but someone proposed one a month ago that was even better:

Pretend the screen is checkerboard colored.

On even turns, monsters on the same color square as the player attack
the player, or try to get closer, while monsters on opposite colored
squares attack some nearby non-player monster if available, the player
if no monster is available but the player is, and make a random move
otherwise.

On odd turns, swap the effect to the other colored squares.

This makes the ring of conflict still cause dissention among the monsters,
but the player no longer gets off scott free.  It is easy to implement,
and restores a lot of game balance.

